  "rationale": {
    "nixos_nft_compat": "Original firewall-start uses fixed iptables-nft 1.8.13, including pkttype, conntrack and rpfilter --validmark. The exact upstream add_match native cases are limit/among/udp/tcp/mark; other names use the match expression and existing x_tables implementations. Existing R4 xt matches are already enabled. The extension xlate callback is not this installation path.",
    "nura_nftables": "Original inet stateful rules and seven included snippets require the nftables core, inet family, conntrack and reject. Named counters/meta/payload/sets are core objects. All original service files/runlevel entries are retained.",
    "nura_zram": "Original deviceinfo does not override the zram algorithm; zramstart explicitly selects zstd. Enable its backend while preserving existing LZO backend and lzo-rle kernel default. FORCE_LZO automatically becomes n.",
    "qemu_rtc": "The retained earlier Alpine builder VM serial registered rtc-pl031 9010000.pl031 as rtc0. R4 lacks RTC_DRV_PL031. Original Nura hwclock uses the RTC but can return zero after failure; a new guest needs actual driver/readback checks. The old serial is only model evidence, not acceptance of Nura or R5."
  },
